[2026-04-05 15:21:55] Expanded the SYSCTL roadmap to implement both USER_REG and BOOTCFG after the user asked to do both remaining SYSCTL families.
Request: yes please do both.
Interpretation: Continue inside SYSCTL by implementing both the USER_REG family and the BOOTCFG family.
Investigation summary: Manual review confirmed USER_REG0-3 and BOOTCFG are documented in Chapter 8 Internal Memory, section 8.6 Memory Register Descriptions (System Control Offset). USER_REG0-3 are readable staged values with restricted non-volatile programming semantics, while BOOTCFG is read-only through SYSCTL and should not gain a public writer in this layer.
Decision: Add a read-only USER_REG getter family and a read-only BOOTCFG field getter family only. Preserve flash-programming and commit behavior outside the SYSCTL public surface.
